---
source: src/main.rs
expression: "render_help_snapshot(&[\"inbox\", \"wait\"])"
---
Wait for an email to reach an inbox, then print it, its code, or its link

Usage: hooklistener inbox wait [OPTIONS] <INBOX>

Arguments:
  <INBOX>  Inbox ID, slug, or address; a plus address such as signup+run42@hookinbox.com also sets
           --to

Options:
      --to <ADDRESS>             Recipient address, exact and case-insensitive, such as a per-run
                                 plus address
      --from <TEXT>              Text the sender contains, case-insensitive
      --subject-contains <TEXT>  Text the subject contains, case-insensitive
      --since <WHEN>             Match emails received after this: an RFC 3339 time, an email ID, or
                                 a duration ago such as 90s or 5m [default: now]
      --timeout <DURATION>       Maximum wait, such as 90, 5m, or 1h (up to 1h) [default: 2m]
      --code                     Print only the one-time code
      --link                     Print only the verification or magic link
  -o, --org <ORG_ID>             Organization ID (overrides the configured default)
  -h, --help                     Print help (see more with '--help')

Global options:
      --json               Output supported command responses or event streams as JSON
      --color <COLOR>      Styling policy for human output [default: auto] [possible values: auto,
                           always, never]
      --yes                Confirm destructive commands without an interactive prompt
      --log-level <LEVEL>  Log level [default: info] [possible values: trace, debug, info, warn,
                           error]
      --log-dir <DIR>      Directory for log files
      --log-stdout         Also write logs to stdout

Without --since, only emails that arrive after the command starts match:
start it before triggering the email, or pass --since.

EXIT STATUS:
  0  An email matched and was printed
  5  --timeout passed before a matching email arrived
  6  The email that matched has no code (--code) or link (--link)
  1  Any other error (2 for invalid arguments)

EXAMPLE:
  ADDR="signup+$RUN_ID@hookinbox.com"
  STARTED=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)
  ./sign-up.sh "$ADDR"
  CODE=$(hooklistener inbox wait "$ADDR" --since "$STARTED" --code)
